{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe Cloud Jira adapter still carries two dead private helpers. backend.py::_fit_description no longer has an executable consumer because the live send-path composition moved to the shared OutboundFieldMapper built with AdfCodec. acli_rest.py::_direct_rest_put also has no production caller and preserves the wrong issue-property envelope shape; the live issue-property, reporter, parent, and unassign flows already use concrete raw PUT writes instead.\n\nBecause both helpers are named in docstrings and held-out inventories, this cleanup must remove the dead code and retarget every surviving prose/test consumer to the real owners rather than leaving dangling references.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. Remove backend.py::_fit_description and keep Cloud description composition owned by the shared OutboundFieldMapper plus RichTextCodec path.\n2. Update every prose/test consumer that still names _fit_description: adapters/jira/jira_fields.py, adapters/jira_family/rich_text.py, adapters/jira/backend.py comment prose, and tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_rich_text_seam_heldout.py.\n3. Remove acli_rest.py::_direct_rest_put and keep set_issue_property, set_reporter, set_parent, and unassign semantics on the concrete raw PUT implementations already used in production.\n4. Update every stale _direct_rest_put consumer or inventory: adapters/jira/acli_rest.py comments, adapters/jira/acli.py unassign prose, tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_cloud_rate_limit_sweep_heldout.py, and tests/scripts/bridge/test_jira_capability_probe.py.\n5. Re-run focused Jira adapter/rich-text/raw-PUT suites, then lint, typecheck, and the default make test selector, treating test_atomic_completion_close::test_relevant_remote_rejection_never_places_candidate_on_shared_head as the known pre-existing baseline failure if it is the only remaining broad-suite miss.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/backend.py\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/jira_fields.py\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/rich_text.py\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_rest.py\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py\n- tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_rich_text_seam_heldout.py\n- tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_cloud_rate_limit_sweep_heldout.py\n- tests/scripts/bridge/test_jira_capability_probe.py\n\n## Testing\n\nRun focused rich-text seam, raw-PUT transport, Cloud unassign, capability-probe, and Jira adapter inventory suites; then run make lint, make typecheck, and pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -x -q.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] backend.py::_fit_description is removed.\n- [x] Cloud rich-text prose points at the shared OutboundFieldMapper plus RichTextCodec composition instead of the deleted helper.\n- [x] test_rich_text_seam_heldout.py guards the helper-name cleanup while preserving the send-path composition oracle.\n- [x] acli_rest.py::_direct_rest_put is removed.\n- [x] Issue-property, reporter, parent, and unassign paths still use the concrete raw PUT writes they used before the cleanup.\n- [x] The stale _direct_rest_put inventory/mock sites in test_cloud_rate_limit_sweep_heldout.py and test_jira_capability_probe.py are updated.\n- [x] Focused Jira adapter/rich-text/raw-PUT suites pass.\n- [x] make lint and make typecheck pass.\n- [x] pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -x -q fails only on the known pre-existing atomic completion baseline test."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788456882410872001,"uuid":"104da43d-2112-481e-93e8-bdbc264bfeab"}